-- title:
--   Mod p eigenform from a maximal Hecke ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, $N'$ a nonzero level, $S_0\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ a set of primes-to-be-avoided containing $p$, and $k\in\mathbb{Z}$ with $k\ge 2$; assume `HasIntegralStructure N' k`, i.e. the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N' k`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spanned by the cusp forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N')$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers spans the whole complex space. Let $i\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $\mathfrak{m}_k$ be a maximal ideal of `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of that cusp-form space generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N'$, $\ell\notin S_0$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N'$, $q\notin S_0$), such that $p\in\mathfrak{m}_k$ and, for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ and $\ell\nmid\Delta_W$, one has $T_\ell-\ell^i a_\ell(W)\in\mathfrak{m}_k$, where $a_\ell(W)=\ell+1-\#W_{/\mathbb{F}_\ell}$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. Then there are a power series $\varphi$ over $F=\overline{\mathbb{F}_p}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Z}/p$) and a function $\lambda:\mathbb{N}\to F$ such that: $\varphi$ lies in `modPCusp N' k F`, the $F$-span of the reductions $\sum_n (a_n \bmod p)q^n$ of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N')$; $\varphi\ne 0$ and for every prime $\ell\nmid N'$ with $\ell\notin S_0$ the coefficient-side Hecke operator with $n$-th coefficient $\operatorname{coeff}_{n\ell}\varphi+[\ell\mid n]\,\ell^{k-1}\operatorname{coeff}_{n/\ell}\varphi$ sends $\varphi$ to $\lambda(\ell)\varphi$; and $\lambda(\ell)=\ell^i a_\ell(W)$ in $F$ for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ and $\ell\nmid\Delta_W$.
--
--   This is the passage, in the style of Deligne–Serre, from a maximal ideal of an integral Hecke algebra whose residue characteristic is $p$ and whose Hecke eigensystem away from $S_0$ and the level is $\ell\mapsto\ell^i a_\ell(W)$, to an actual nonzero mod $p$ cusp form with that eigensystem. It feeds the weight- and level-manipulation steps for the Frey curve, being cited by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_three_weight_le_four_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_three_weight_le_four_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two) and [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_of_pow_mul_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_of_pow_mul_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
